  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Think-and-Do-Tank to accelerate resilience building in Arid and Semi Arid Lands  (ASALS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Think and Do Tank in accelerating  resilience building in the Arid and Semi-Arid  Lands (ASALS) is a 3 year project with a budget of Euro 1 million. The project aim is to strengthen decision-making on climate resilient approaches mainly policies, interventions and investments. This will be achieved through collating ,synthesizing  and brokering data, processes and practices targeting arid and semi-arid land (ASALs).This activity will see strengthened capacity of county governments in mainstreaming  climate adaptation in development work and increased private sector engagement. Results will  include an interactive data platform, investment opportunity  profiles for viable climate-smart  value chains, information brokering for private sector and county governments to make better investment decisions for resilience building. The project will target 8 ASAL counties: Laikipia, Isiolo, Samburu, Narok, Kajiado, Taita Taveta, Turkana and Marsabit.</narrative>
  </description>
